{"id":"torrey:murder","source":"torrey","name":"Murder","slug":"murder","seeAlso":[],"entries":[{"text":"Forbidden by Mosaic law — Ex 20:13; De 5:17.","refs":[["Exod",20,13,20,13],["Deut",5,17,5,17]]},{"text":"Why forbidden by God — Ge 9:6.","refs":[["Gen",9,6,9,6]]},{"text":"The law made to restrain — 1Ti 1:9.","refs":[["1Tim",1,9,1,9]]},{"text":"With premeditation. — Ex 21:14.","refs":[["Exod",21,14,21,14]]},{"text":"From hatred. — Nu 35:20,21; De 19:11.","refs":[["Num",35,20,35,20],["Num",35,21,35,21],["Deut",19,11,19,11]]},{"text":"By lying in wait. — Nu 35:20; De 19:11.","refs":[["Num",35,20,35,20],["Deut",19,11,19,11]]},{"text":"By an instrument of iron. — Nu 35:16.","refs":[["Num",35,16,35,16]]},{"text":"By the blow of a stone. — Nu 35:17.","refs":[["Num",35,17,35,17]]},{"text":"By a hand weapon of wood. — Nu 35:18.","refs":[["Num",35,18,35,18]]},{"text":"Killing a thief in the day, counted as — Ex 22:3.","refs":[["Exod",22,3,22,3]]},{"text":"Early introduction of — Ge 4:8.","refs":[["Gen",4,8,4,8]]},{"text":"Represented as a sin crying to heaven — Ge 4:10; Heb 12:24; Re 6:10.","refs":[["Gen",4,10,4,10],["Heb",12,24,12,24],["Rev",6,10,6,10]]},{"text":"The Jews often guilty of — Isa 1:21.","refs":[["Isa",1,21,1,21]]},{"text":"Fearful and cowardly. — Ge 4:14.","refs":[["Gen",4,14,4,14]]},{"text":"Wanderers and vagabonds. — Ge 4:14.","refs":[["Gen",4,14,4,14]]},{"text":"Flee from God’s presence. — Ge 4:16.","refs":[["Gen",4,16,4,16]]},{"text":"Not protected in refuge cities. — De 19:11,12.","refs":[["Deut",19,11,19,11],["Deut",19,12,19,12]]},{"text":"Had no protection from altars. — Ex 21:14.","refs":[["Exod",21,14,21,14]]},{"text":"Not to be pitied or spared. — De 19:13.","refs":[["Deut",19,13,19,13]]},{"text":"Often committed by night — Ne 6:10; Job 24:14.","refs":[["Neh",6,10,6,10],["Job",24,14,24,14]]},{"text":"Imputed to the nearest city when the murderer was unknown — De 21:1-3.","refs":[["Deut",21,1,21,3]]},{"text":"Mode of clearing those suspected of — D